<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Pangenome primer design results</title>
<style>
  :root {
    --pass:#1a7f37; --dropout:#cf222e; --off_target:#bc4c00;
    --multi_product:#8250df; --uncertain:#6e7781; --bg:#fff; --fg:#1f2328; --line:#d0d7de;
  }
  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
    :root { --bg:#0d1117; --fg:#e6edf3; --line:#30363d; }
  }
  body { font-family: system-ui, sans-serif; margin: 2rem; background: var(--bg); color: var(--fg); }
  h1 { font-size: 1.4rem; } h2 { font-size: 1.1rem; margin-top: 2rem; }
  .wrap { overflow-x: auto; }
  table { border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 0.85rem; }
  th, td { border: 1px solid var(--line); padding: 4px 8px; text-align: left; white-space: nowrap; }
  .cell { width: 1.5rem; height: 1.5rem; text-align: center; color: #fff; font-weight: 600; }
  .pass{background:var(--pass)} .dropout{background:var(--dropout)}
  .off_target{background:var(--off_target)} .multi_product{background:var(--multi_product)}
  .uncertain{background:var(--uncertain)}
  .passed { color: var(--pass); font-weight: 700; }
  .failed { color: var(--dropout); font-weight: 700; }
  .legend span { display:inline-block; padding:2px 8px; border-radius:3px; color:#fff; margin-right:6px; font-size:.8rem; }
  code { font-size: 0.8rem; }
  .muted { color: var(--uncertain); font-size: 0.8rem; }
  .glossary { margin: 1rem 0; font-size: 0.85rem; }
  .glossary summary { cursor: pointer; font-weight: 600; }
  .glossary dl { display: grid; grid-template-columns: max-content 1fr; gap: 4px 16px; margin: 0.6rem 0; }
  .glossary dt { font-weight: 700; font-family: ui-monospace, monospace; white-space: nowrap; }
  .glossary dd { margin: 0; }
  .glossary span { padding: 1px 5px; border-radius: 3px; color: #fff; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<h1>Pangenome PCR primer design — results</h1>
<p class="legend">
  {% for s in statuses %}<span class="{{ s }}">{{ s }}</span>{% endfor %}
</p>
{% if data.provenance %}
<p class="muted">Provenance:
  {% for k, v in data.provenance.items() %}<code>{{ k }}={{ v }}</code>&nbsp;{% endfor %}
</p>
{% endif %}

<details class="glossary">
<summary>Column &amp; status definitions</summary>
<dl>
  <dt>coverage</dt><dd><b>On-target coverage</b> — fraction of <i>evaluable</i> haplotypes that produce the intended target amplicon at all (≥1 on-target band: <span class="pass">pass</span> or <span class="multi_product">multi_product</span> that includes an on-target band). The anti-dropout metric: "does the target amplify across diversity?"</dd>
  <dt>unique</dt><dd><b>Unique product rate</b> — fraction of evaluable haplotypes that give exactly one product and it is the on-target one, no off-target (i.e. <span class="pass">pass</span>). The specificity metric: "is the reaction clean?" Coverage can be high while this is low.</dd>
  <dt>eval</dt><dd><b>Evaluable</b> haplotypes = total − uncertain. All fractions use this as the denominator.</dd>
  <dt>uncertain</dt><dd>Haplotypes where the locus is broken/unmappable in the assembly; excluded from the denominator, never counted as failure.</dd>
  <dt>dropout</dt><dd>Haplotypes where the target should amplify but a binding-site SNP/indel prevents it (no on-target product).</dd>
  <dt>off-target</dt><dd>Haplotypes whose single product forms outside the expected homologous locus.</dd>
  <dt>multi</dt><dd>Haplotypes with more than one product (extra bands), on- and/or off-target.</dd>
  <dt>penalty</dt><dd>Primer3 pair penalty (thermodynamic/design quality; lower is better). Used only as a tie-break among passing pairs.</dd>
  <dt>product bp</dt><dd>Designed amplicon size on the CHM13 template.</dd>
</dl>
<p class="muted">Matrix cell letters: <b>P</b>=pass, <b>D</b>=dropout, <b>O</b>=off_target, <b>M</b>=multi_product, <b>U</b>=uncertain. Hover a cell for the reason.</p>
</details>

<h2>Ranked primer pairs</h2>
<div class="wrap">
<table>
  <tr>
    <th>pair</th><th>verdict</th><th>coverage</th><th>unique</th>
    <th>eval</th><th>uncertain</th><th>dropout</th><th>off-target</th><th>multi</th>
    <th>penalty</th><th>product bp</th>
  </tr>
  {% for p in data.pairs %}
  <tr>
    <td><code>{{ p.name }}</code></td>
    <td class="{{ 'passed' if p.passed else 'failed' }}">{{ 'PASS' if p.passed else 'reject' }}</td>
    <td>{{ '%.1f%%' % (p.on_target_coverage * 100) }}</td>
    <td>{{ '%.1f%%' % (p.unique_product_rate * 100) }}</td>
    <td>{{ p.n_evaluable }}</td><td>{{ p.n_uncertain }}</td>
    <td>{{ p.n_dropout }}</td><td>{{ p.n_off_target }}</td><td>{{ p.n_multi_product }}</td>
    <td>{{ '%.2f' % p.primer3_penalty }}</td><td>{{ p.product_size_chm13 }}</td>
  </tr>
  {% if not p.passed and p.reject_reasons %}
  <tr><td colspan="11" class="muted">rejected: {{ p.reject_reasons | join('; ') }}</td></tr>
  {% endif %}
  {% endfor %}
</table>
</div>

<h2>Per-haplotype status matrix</h2>
<div class="wrap">
<table>
  <tr><th>pair \ haplotype</th>{% for h in hap_order %}<th>{{ h }}</th>{% endfor %}</tr>
  {% for p in data.pairs %}
  <tr>
    <td><code>{{ p.name }}</code></td>
    {% for h in hap_order %}
      {% set cell = status_map[p.name][h] %}
      <td class="cell {{ cell.status }}" title="{{ cell.reason }}">{{ cell.status[0]|upper }}</td>
    {% endfor %}
  </tr>
  {% endfor %}
</table>
</div>
<p class="muted">Cell letter: P=pass, D=dropout, O=off_target, M=multi_product, U=uncertain. Hover for the reason.</p>
</body>
</html>
